      {
        "number": 8,
        "internalPageId": null,
        "title": "Structures Examples Observations 1 Have someone do something Will you have Jade do the dinner? They have had Ericka clean the house for years. Have + N + V (simple form) This may vary depending on the tenses. 2 Have something done She *got her eyes operated last week. They will have the car fixed by noon. Have + N + V (Past participle) This may vary depending on the tenses. 3 Get someone / Something to ... My dad got Jane to teach me math. I have gotten Annie to buy the apartment. She finally crossed the Rubicon. Get + N + Non-finite clause",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "Structures Examples Observations 1 Have someone do something Will you have Jade do the dinner? They have had Ericka clean the house for years. Have + N + V (simple form) This may vary depending on the tenses. 2 Have something done She *got her eyes operated last week. They will have the car fixed by noon. Have + N + V (Past participle) This may vary depending on the tenses. 3 Get someone / Something to ... My dad got Jane to teach me math. I have gotten Annie to buy the apartment. She finally crossed the Rubicon. Get + N + Non-finite clause",
          "There are many ways in which we can say someone does something for us or in our behalf; however, check this chart to learn a new one where we work with causative."
        ],
        "links": [],
        "media": [
